      "dom_id": "question-79466",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=2x+4c\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $c$ are real numbers.",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=2x+4c\\text{i},$ we have $a=2x$ and $b=4c.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|2x+4c\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+(4c)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+16{c}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
