      "problem": "What is the magnitude of the number $z=2\\text{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The imaginary number $2\\text{i}$ is equivalent to the complex number $z=0+2\\text{i}.$\n\nWe know that for a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of $z=0+2\\text{i}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z| & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
